      "cr": 0.5,
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>Era sheet: 18 Harvestide, 1035 BF, Bowser's Castle.</em> Art and stats describe this figure on the night the castle came down (events.json <code>bowser_throne_room_compromise</code> and <code>the_assault_on_bowsers_castle</code>), not the present day of the campaign (1040 BF).</p><p><strong>Session kit — The Castle Comes Down (Session III).</strong> A GM kit for the night after the breach, not a filed event; nothing on this sheet changes the canon record. The run-sheet is <code>docs/sessions/bowsers-castle-1035-the-castle-comes-down.md</code>.</p><p>Not a traitor — a soldier somebody else is driving. The record says the hypnotised soldiers were defeated by coordination rather than by one heroic strike: shell barriers made a lane, Goombas pulled at legs and belts, and the garrison took its own people down without killing them. The sheet makes that the rule.</p><p><em>From the record:</em> 'The hypnotised soldiers were defeated by coordination.'</p>",
        "public": ""
      }
